uth Organization  they use us thank you so much for  joining us this morning was she right to  resign I think it was a consequential  step of Angela marichuy oh and they're  not as to resign because the criticism  of her was really big in the last weeks  and I think even though she offered to  have re-elections at the parliamentary  group on Tuesday I think that would have  not silenced the voices of criticism but  I think also that the pressure was  really really high on her and they was  quite unfair actually and to blame her  as a person for the results of the  European election and she actually said  when she you know announced this that  the party needs to regain the trust and  the respect for one another  did the SPD treat its leader badly I  think for some factors was it was unfair  and I think that she suffered from  criticism because she was not so popular  and she's a character which is not so  common in politics because you know  sometimes she's just really yeah a  character you know she does things that  are not really common but I think also  that politics needs some people who are  like do unexpected things or have some  comments which is I think it's nice to  have people like that but I also think  that she did do some mistakes and I  think that we need change in the  leadership but just one person it's not  gonna do the deal ultimately it was her  who persuaded the party to join Merkel's  coalition government last year a very  you know we know that your party wanted  to enter the opposition for example what  happens to the coalition now we really  don't know and we use this the youth  organization we pushed for the  affiliation of the coalition  our Party Congress in December so I  think we need to pull that forward and  do that earlier this year actually and  we need our party Congress earlier than  December we need a reelection of the  party board and we need that affiliation  of the grand coalition really soon  because honestly it's a grand coalit